#!/bin/sh
# Gate: commits touching shared headway/tier pipeline logic must record a
# validation status, even when the honest answer is "not applicable."
#
# Why: AI-217 (Halifax route 330, single agency) generalized an unvalidated
# fix into process-core.ts's all-agency headway computation. f9001a4f
# repeated the same pattern two days later on a single TTC case. The two
# stacked and broke on 32 routes across 18 French cities before anyone
# noticed (issue #263). Neither commit had a test or any record of checking
# another agency. This hook exists so that decision gets written down
# somewhere durable instead of only in an ephemeral chat session.
#
# List extended 2026-07-25 after an audit found the same pattern already live
# in pipeline/shape-selection.ts (commit 1eafd76a generalized a single
# Rennes-route fix into shared shape-selection logic with no test), and added
# transit-corridors.ts (shares transit-calendar.ts's gated logic, zero test
# coverage) and parseGtfs.ts (global shape-correction logic, high blast
# radius) as structural risks of the same shape even without a confirmed
# incident yet.

msg_file="$1"

GATED_FILES='pipeline/process-core.ts
pipeline/headway-utils.ts
pipeline/transit-calendar.ts
pipeline/transit-phase1.ts
pipeline/transit-phase2.ts
pipeline/shape-selection.ts
pipeline/transit-corridors.ts
pipeline/parseGtfs.ts'

staged=$(git diff --cached --name-only)

touched=""
for f in $GATED_FILES; do
  if echo "$staged" | grep -qx "$f"; then
    touched="$touched $f"
  fi
done

[ -z "$touched" ] && exit 0

# Satisfied if a regression test changed alongside it...
if echo "$staged" | grep -q '^pipeline/__tests__/'; then
  exit 0
fi

# ...or the commit message explicitly records validation status.
if grep -qiE '^Validated:' "$msg_file"; then
  exit 0
fi

cat <<EOF
commit-msg: blocked — this commit touches shared pipeline logic every agency runs through:
$touched

That code path has a history of single-agency reports becoming unvalidated
app-wide changes (AI-217 -> f9001a4f -> issue #263: broke on 32 routes
across 18 French cities before anyone noticed). This gate exists so that
doesn't happen silently again.

Add ONE of the following before committing:
  1. A regression test under pipeline/__tests__/ covering the change, or
  2. A "Validated:" line in the commit message, e.g.:
       Validated: TTC, Rennes, Bordeaux, Dijon
       Validated: n/a - pure refactor, no calculation change
       Validated: n/a - reverts <hash>

This is a record-keeping gate, not a review gate — "n/a" with a real reason
is a legitimate answer. The point is that the decision is written down, not
that every change needs a full audit.
EOF
exit 1
